findings.body:
The hook restores the default favicon on unmount using `/favicon-16x16.png` and `/favicon-32x32.png` (plus the `-dark` variants). Those files are not in `ui-v2/public/`. The real assets live under `public/ico/`, and `index.html` links them from there (`/ico/favicon-16x16.png`, and so on). So after leaving a task run page, the favicon `href` is set to a 404, and the browser tab icon breaks until a full reload.

The reset should restore the same paths that `index.html` declares, or better, save each element's original `href` before the first change and put that value back.

::diff{file="ui-v2/src/hooks/use-state-favicon.ts" lines="55-64"}

::callout{type="warning"}
This is not caught by the PR's own checklist. The Vue app and any direct navigation will show the bug only after the user leaves a task run page.

`StateType` includes `CANCELLING` and `PAUSED`, and the hook builds the path as `/${stateType.toLowerCase()}.svg` for any truthy state. The PR only adds SVGs for cancelled, completed, crashed, failed, pending, running and scheduled. For a task run in CANCELLING or PAUSED, the hook sets the favicon to `/cancelling.svg` or `/paused.svg`, and both return 404. The checklist already notes these states are unhandled, but the code does not guard against them, so the browser ends up with a broken icon instead of keeping the default.

A small allowlist, or a fallback to the default icon for unknown states, would avoid the 404.

::diff{file="ui-v2/src/hooks/use-state-favicon.ts" lines="49-53"}

The sidebar uses a truthy check for `retry_jitter_factor`. The API type is `number | null` (see `ui-v2/src/api/prefect.ts:10859`), and `0` is a valid value that means "no jitter". With this change, a task run with `retry_jitter_factor: 0` shows "None", while the old code rendered "0". So the PR introduces a regression in a field it was meant to make more accurate.

The same pattern is used for `cache_key` and `dynamic_key`, which are strings, so an empty string is the only falsy case there. Those checks are fine. For numbers, use a null and undefined check, as the duration and estimated-run-time fields already do.

::diff{file="ui-v2/src/components/task-runs/task-run-details/task-run-details.tsx" lines="177-182"}
